_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.5.1, 4.4, 4.3, 4.2, 4.2-dev2\n- Not reproducible in: 4.2-dev1 and earlier versions\n- Not reproducible in: 4.5.1 - Web\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9144) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-13700H (20 threads) - 63.70 Gio memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen clicking on a button to change scene with a touchscreen, the following error appears in the debugger : \n\n```\nE 0:00:02:384   can_process: Condition \"!is_inside_tree()\" is true. Returning: false\n  <Source C++>  scene/main/node.cpp:889 @ can_process()\n\n```\n\nThis error points to the source file line :  [https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/f62fdbde15035c5576dad93e586201f4d41ef0cb/scene/main/node.cpp#L889](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/f62fdbde15035c5576dad93e586201f4d41ef0cb/scene/main/node.cpp#L889)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a scene with a Node2D\n2. Create another scene woth a Control node\n3. Attach a script to the Control node\n4. Add a child Button node and make it bigger to be able to click on it\n5. Connect the on_pressed signal to the script\n7. Add the following code to the method\n```gdscript\nget_tree().change_scene_to_file(\"res://node_2d.tscn\")\n```\n8. Play the control.tscn scene\n9. Click on the button using the touchscreen\n\nThe error should appear in debugger console.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp-v4.5.1.stable.official-\\[f62fdbde1\\].zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24849696/mrp-v4.5.1.stable.official-.f62fdbde1.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_ur